## Mutation verification (each defect reintroduced individually, then reverted)

# A — restore the teaching-blind literal at the _sessionStart re-arm site
#     `if (_shouldResumeGuidedTopic())` -> `if (!_s.guidedTopic && _s._guidedTopicInFlight)`
# -> Tests: 3 failed, 43 passed, 46 total
# -> outputs/jest-mutation-A-teaching-blind-rearm.txt

# B — re-nest the delivered flag inside the one-shot guidedAutoClose block
# -> Tests: 3 failed, 43 passed, 46 total
# -> outputs/jest-mutation-B-delivered-flag-renested.txt

# C — neuter the completion crediting: `if (false && _s._guidedTopicInFlight && ...)`
# -> FIRST RUN: 46 passed — the mutation was NOT caught. The assertion matched a
#    substring of the condition, so a disabled gate passed. Real hole in this
#    VTID's own tests, found by running the mutation rather than assuming it.
#    Assertion tightened to pin the whole condition anchored on `if (` and `) {`.
# -> RE-RUN: Tests: 1 failed, 13 passed, 14 total
# -> outputs/jest-mutation-C-no-completion-crediting.txt

